  url={https://aclanthology.org/2026.semeval-1.197/},
  abstract={A multi-seed DeBERTa ensemble for political response clarity and evasion classification: 5-fold cross-validation with 10 random seeds yields 50 models per architecture, combined through logit averaging. The system achieves macro F1 of 0.76 on clarity (18/41) and 0.50 on evasion (12/33). Three post-hoc optimization techniques each improve out-of-fold performance yet degrade evaluation scores, suggesting a risk of overfitting to cross-validation predictions when evaluation data is limited.},
